Alembic Database Migrations
============================

This directory contains Alembic migration scripts for the ModelPrism backend.

Prerequisites
-------------
- Python 3.11+ with dependencies installed (see requirements.txt or pyproject.toml)
- A running PostgreSQL instance
- A valid .env file in backend/ with DATABASE_URL set

Commands
--------
  # Apply all pending migrations:
  alembic upgrade head

  # Roll back the most recent migration:
  alembic downgrade -1

  # Generate a new migration automatically (from model changes):
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description of changes"

  # Preview the SQL that would be generated (offline mode):
  alembic upgrade head --sql

Architecture
------------
- Migrations use the async SQLAlchemy engine from app.database.
- The env.py reads the database URL from app.config.settings at runtime.
- Each migration is a single Python file in the versions/ directory.
- Never edit a migration that has already been applied to production.
  Create a new migration instead.
